
 Post-install setup for rda_python_metrics setuid programs.

 logarch runs as the common user gdexdata via the rda_python_setuid mechanism.
 Follow the steps below after pip install to complete the setup.

 Dependency: rda_python_setuid is declared as a dependency of this package
 and is installed automatically with pip install rda_python_metrics.

 Environment setup:

   Option A - Python venv (recommended for DECS machines):

      python3 -m venv $ENVHOME          # e.g. /glade/u/home/gdexdata/gdexmsenv
      source $ENVHOME/bin/activate
      pip install rda_python_metrics

   Option B - Conda (recommended for DAV/Casper):

      conda activate pg-gdex            # e.g. /glade/work/gdexdata/conda-envs/pg-gdex
      pip install rda_python_metrics

 Full setuid install (requires sudo access to gdexdata):

   Run these steps once per environment after pip install:

   1. Compile the pywrapper C binary (once per environment):
         pywrapper-install -u gdexdata

   2. Wire up logarch as a setuid entry:
         pywrapper-install -l logarch -u gdexdata

 Simple install (no sudo required, runs as current user):

   pywrapper-install -l logarch -s

   This creates bin/logarch -> bin/setuid_logarch and logarch runs as the
   current user with no privilege change.

 After setup, run logarch with no arguments to display its user guide.
